&lt;p&gt;Please join the Harriman Institute for a book talk by&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Egana Djabbarova&lt;/strong&gt;. Moderated by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://harriman.columbia.edu/person/mark-lipovetsky/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mark Lipovetsky&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Egana Djabbarova discusses her dazzling debut novel &amp;quot;MY DREADFUL BODY&amp;quot; about a young woman&amp;#39;s vexed coming of age in a traditional Azerbaijani community in Russia, grappling under the weight of Muslim patriarchal norms and a debilitating neurological condition. The mysterious affliction leaves her unable to control her muscles, plagued by pain and speech disorders. Addressing each body part with the scrupulousness of a medical researcher, the narrator explores memories, traditions, and taboos related to her physical self. Egana Djabbarova unveils a hidden world in which illness unexpectedly facilitates her liberation from the fate of an arranged marriage she doesn&amp;#39;t want.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please email&amp;nbsp;disability@columbia.edu&amp;nbsp;to request disability accommodations. Advance notice is necessary to arrange for some accessibility needs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Join us for an evening with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Olga Ravn&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;as part of Columbia&amp;rsquo;s Art + Life series, a programme of intimate conversations with poets and writers organized&amp;nbsp;by Columbia&amp;rsquo;s Undergraduate Creative Writing Program&amp;nbsp;for majors and aficionados. Art + Life has hosted writers like Ladan Osman, Hernan Diaz, Phillip B. Williams, Bushra Rehman, Morgan Parker, Tommy Pico, Jenny Zhang, Eileen Myles and many others, and provides an opportunity for students to ask the invited reader questions and to engage in roundtable discussions with the artist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Olga Ravn&amp;nbsp;(b. 1986) is a Danish novelist and poet. In collaboration with Danish publisher Gyldendal she edited a selection of Tove Ditlevsen&amp;rsquo;s texts and books that relaunched Ditlevsen&amp;rsquo;s readership worldwide. Her novel&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;The Employees&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;was on the shortlist for the Booker Prize in 2021, and her novel The Wax Child was published by New Directions in 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ravn will be in conversation with Associate Professor of Writing, &lt;a href="https://arts.columbia.edu/profiles/rivka-galchen" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rivka Galchen&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hosted by the &lt;a href="https://datascience.columbia.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;Data Science Institute&lt;/a&gt; at Columbia University&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.daxnyc.ai/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DAX: Data Science and AI Exchange 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsible AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is advancing at an ever faster pace. It is impacting virtually every aspect of business. DAX brings together leaders from academia, industry and government for an exchange of perspectives and thoughtful dialog on both the opportunities and challenges of deploying AI responsibly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsible AI builds confidence across the broader ecosystem and creates the conditions for sustainable innovation, risk management, and long-term value. DAX 2026 will explore how these principles are being translated into practice, highlighting the research and ideas that enable organizations to harness AI&amp;#39;s power responsibly. The event will conclude with an Innovation Showcase featuring the latest research from several of Columbia&amp;rsquo;s labs as well as AI focused start-ups spun out from the university.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.daxnyc.ai/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DAX: Data Science and AI Exchange&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;is Columbia University&amp;rsquo;s flagship event for industry executives seeking direct insight into where AI is headed and the research shaping what comes next. Designed as an exchange between industry and university leaders on pressing AI challenges, DAX offers attendees an inside look at emerging work in domains that matter most to business. Through cross-sector dialogue and applied examples, DAX connects cutting-edge developments with real-world strategic opportunities. Additionally, the Innovation Showcase features a glimpse of what is to come with research presentations and demos from Columbia AI start-ups.&lt;/p&gt;
